      "content": "While some people with asthma manage to take beta-blockers without issue, the risk of bronchospasm, which can lead to an asthma attack, is a known concern. Because every person reacts differently to medications, a generalized risk assessment cannot replace professional medical judgment. I must strongly advise against self-medicating with prescription drugs, even a low dose, due to the unpredictability of how it might affect your lung function.",
